HK_FAQ=[("When does Hanukkah start in 2026?","Hanukkah 2026 begins at sundown on Friday, December 4, 2026, and ends at nightfall on Saturday, December 12, 2026, according to Hebcal. That is Hebrew year 5787, starting on the 25th of Kislev."),
("How many nights is Hanukkah?","Eight nights and eight days. One more candle is lit each night, so the eighth night has all eight candles plus the shamash, the helper candle."),
("When is Hanukkah in 2027 and 2028?","In 2027, the first candle is lit on the evening of Friday, December 24, and the last day is Saturday, January 1, 2028. In 2028, the first candle is on Tuesday, December 12, and the last day is Wednesday, December 20. Dates are from Hebcal."),
("Why does Hanukkah move every year?","Hanukkah always starts on the 25th of Kislev on the Hebrew calendar, which is lunisolar. That date can land anywhere from late November to late December on the regular calendar."),
("How do you light the menorah?","Candles go into the menorah from right to left but are lit from left to right, newest candle first, using the shamash. The blessings are said before lighting. In Ashkenazi homes the shamash is lit first; Sephardi homes use an extra candle and light the shamash last."),
("What happens when Hanukkah overlaps with Shabbat?","Lighting a fire on Shabbat is not allowed under Jewish law, so on Friday the menorah is lit before the Shabbat candles while it is still light out. In 2026 that applies on Dec 4 and Dec 11. On Saturday night, Dec 5, lighting waits until Shabbat ends."),
("How many candles do you need for all eight nights?","44 per menorah, counting the shamash each night.")]
